Insert Objects into the Scene
You can insert objects into the 3D scene from the Toolbox or the Class Library. They contain the same
objects by default.
Proceed as follows:
• To insert an object from the Toolbox, click the object you want to insert with the left mouse button and
drag the mouse to the position in the 3D window at which you want to place the object. Click the mouse
button to insert the object. Cancel inserting by clicking the right mouse button or by pressing Esc.
• To insert an object from the Class Library, click the object you want to insert with the left mouse
button, hold down the mouse button and drag the mouse to the position in the 3D window at which
you want to place the object. Then, release the mouse button. As long as you do not release the mouse
button, Plant Simulation shows a preview of the object in the 3D window. You can cancel inserting by
releasing the mouse outside of the 3D window.
• To insert an object which you copied with Home > Copy or with Ctrl+C to the Clipboard, press Ctrl+V in
the 3D window to paste the copy into the object opened in the 3D window. Plant Simulation pastes the
copy at the same position which the copied object takes within its location.
To insert an object from the Toolbox:
• If you want the object to snap to the closest intersection of two grid lines of where you click the mouse
button, click 
  on the Edit ribbon tab.
If you want to place the object freely, do not click 
 . Plant Simulation snaps the object according to
the settings for aligning to the grid or for aligning the object to the grid and/or to objects.
Note
When you insert Markers into your model, make sure that the Markers are aligned. This prevents
Plant Simulation from computing unnecessary roundings between the Markers. Misaligned Markers
might occur if you inserted Markers into your model while Show Grid was off.
• Click the object you want to insert with the left mouse button to select it. Then, drag the mouse to the
location where you want to place it and release and click the mouse button.
• If need be, you can fine-tune the location of the object in the dialog 3D Properties that clicking 
  on
the Home ribbon tab opens.
• To open the dialog of the simulation object, click the button in the bottom left corner in the dialog 3D
Properties or double-click the object in the 3D scene. Modify settings here.
Insert Objects into the Scene
Plant Simulation Help 10-921
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To insert the same object from the Toolbox into a Frame several times, one after the other without
interruption, hold down Ctrl and select the object. The object remains selected in the Toolbox after
inserting it and you can thus insert several of these objects one after the other. You can exit this mode by
clicking the right mouse button or by pressing Esc.
After you inserted objects into your simulation model, you can align them to the grid 
 , make them
snap to the grid 
 , make them snap to other objects 
 , or arrange them on the grid. To be
able to do so, make sure that Show Grid 
  is on.
See also
Move an Object With the Mouse
Work with the Grid
