Select Objects
You can select objects in the 3D window by clicking it with the left mouse button.
You can:
• Select a simulation object, which is directly located in the object that is opened in the window.
Plant Simulation shows selected simulation objects in green.
• Select an animatable object, which belongs to the simulation object that is opened in the window.
Plant Simulation shows selected animatable objects in purple.
• Select a graphic, which visualizes the simulation object that is opened in the window.
Plant Simulation shows selected graphics in yellow-green.
• Select a displayed manipulator.
• Select two or more items by holding down the Shift or the Ctrl key and clicking the desired elements
with the left mouse button.
• Select several items by dragging a marquee around the desired objects:
◦ When you do not hold down the Shift or the Ctrl key, the selection with a marquee cancels an
existing selection.
◦ When you hold down the Shift or the Ctrl key, the new selection will be added to the existing
selection.
• Press Ctrl+A to select all objects in the scene.
Select Objects
10-922 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

You can modify the selection with the plus-key (+) and the minus key (-), compare the Quick Reference
Card > While Modeling.
To show objects, for example in the statistics report, in the sequence in which you selected them, hold
down Shift and click the objects one after the other. In the example below we first clicked Station1, then
Station2, and then Station3.
Compare Move an Object With the Mouse
Back to Work with Objects
Simultaneously Paste Multiple Copies
At times you may want to paste more than one copy of the object you copied. You might, for example,
want to create a Store with a number of shelves.
To paste multiple copies of an object:
• Insert the object you need, for example a Station, into the scene.
• Select the Station and copy it by pressing Ctrl+C.
• Click Paste > Multiple Paste on the Home ribbon tab.
• Enter the number of Stations you would like to paste into the combo box Count. We entered 4.
Simultaneously Paste Multiple Copies
Plant Simulation Help 10-923
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Enter the Offset of the copies from the object you originally placed. Our Station is 2.0 meters wide:
An offset of 2.0 meters on the X-axis pastes 4 copies of the Station with this Offset to the original
toward the right. Note the initial predefined offset toward the right and downwards. We implemented
this to prevent Plant Simulation from pasting the copies one on top of the other.
Click Paste. If need be, move the pasted copies to where you need them.
A Number of Copies of 4 and an Offset of 2.0 meters on the X-axis and on the Z-axis pastes 4 copies
to the right and up of the original Station.
Click Paste. If need be, move the pasted copies to where you need them.
