Move an Object With Keyboard Keys
Instead of using the mouse to manipulate the selected object, you can also hold down the Ctrl or Shift
keys and press one of the arrow keys on the keyboard.
To move the selected object on the grid plane, press the designated arrow key:
• Press the left arrow to move the object to the left by 10% of the distance set in the dialog Edit Grid and
Base Plate Settings under Grid Lines > Select for Snapping.
Press the left arrow and hold down Shift to move the object to the left by the distance set in the dialog
Edit Grid and Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for Snapping.
• Press the right arrow to move the object to the right by 10% of the distance set in the dialog Edit Grid
and Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for Snapping.
Press the right arrow and hold down Shift to move the object to the right by the distance set in the
dialog Edit Grid and Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for Snapping.
• Press the up arrow to move the object upward by 10% of the distance set in the dialog Edit Grid and
Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for Snapping.
Press the up arrow and hold down Shift to move the object upward by the distance set in the dialog
Edit Grid and Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for Snapping.
• Press the down arrow to move the object downward by 10% of the distance set in the dialog Edit Grid
and Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for Snapping.
Press the down arrow and hold down Shift to move the object downward by the distance set in the
dialog Edit Grid and Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for Snapping.
To move the selected object vertically up or down, hold down Ctrl and press the designated arrow key:
• Hold down Ctrl and press the up arrow to move the object upward in the z-direction by 10% of the
distance set in the dialog Edit Grid and Base Plate Settings
Hold down Shift and Ctrl and press the up arrow to move the object upward in the z-direction by the
distance set in the dialog Edit Grid and Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for Snapping.
• Hold down Ctrl and press the down arrow to move the object downward in the z-direction by 10%
of the distance set in the dialog Edit Grid and Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for
Snapping.
Hold down Shift and Ctrl and press the down arrow to move the object downward in the z-direction
by the distance set in the dialog Edit Grid and Base Plate Settings under Grid lines > Select for
Snapping.
To rotate the selected object, hold down Ctrl and press the designated arrow key:
• Hold down Ctrl and press the left arrow to rotate the object counterclockwise by 1°.
Hold down Shift and Ctrl and press the left arrow to rotate the object counterclockwise by 45°.
Move an Object With Keyboard Keys
10-926 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Hold down Ctrl and press the right arrow to rotate the object clockwise by 1°.
Hold down Shift and Ctrl and press the right arrow to rotate the object clockwise by 45°.
