Move an Object Precisely
At times manually moving an object with the mouse or with keyboard keys will not be accurate enough for
your purposes. Then, you can enter exact values into a dialog.
To do this, enter exact values into the text boxes in the dialog 3D Properties > Tab Transformation to
fine-tune the position, the rotation, and the scale of the selected object:
To precisely move an object:
• Select the object you would like to move.
• Press the spacebar or click 
  on the Home ribbon tab and click the tab Transformation.
• To move the object to the right on the x-axis, click in the text box and roll the mouse wheel forward
to increase the position in steps of 0.1 meters. Hold down Shift and roll the mouse wheel forward to
increase the position in steps of 1 meter.
To move the object to the left on the x-axis, click in the text box and roll the mouse wheel backward
to decrease the position in steps of 0.1 meters. Hold down Shift and roll the mouse wheel forward to
decrease the position in steps of 1 meter.
Move an Object Precisely
Plant Simulation Help 10-927
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Use the same procedure for the y-axis.
• Use the same procedure for the z-axis.
• Click Apply to apply your change and to see if the meet your requirements.
• Click OK once you’re satisfied with the results.
Compare Edit Grouped Graphics
