Rotate Objects in the Scene
Rotate Objects in the Frame
Plant Simulation provides several ways of rotating an object in the 3D window.
You can:
• Rotate an Object with Keyboard Keys
• Rotate an Object Precisely
Rotate an Object with Keyboard Keys
When you manually rotate an object around an axis by holding down Shift+Ctrl and pressing the left
or the right arrow on the keyboard, 3D uses the settings under Rotation in the dialog 3D Properties >
Transformation > Settings for the Rotation. You can either use the default settings or define the settings
that meet your modeling needs.
To manually rotate an object in the 3D window with the settings you define:
• Click 
  on the View ribbon tab to show the grid.
• Click the object you want to rotate.
• To rotate the object by 1° to the left, hold down Ctrl and press the left arrow.
To rotate the object by 1° to the right, hold down Ctrl and press the right arrow.
• To rotate the object by 45° to the left, hold down Ctrl and the Shift and press the left arrow.
To rotate the object by 45° to the right, hold down Ctrl and Shift and press the right arrow.
• To rotate the object by 10° on the x-axis to the left, press 7 on the numeric keypad.
To rotate the object by 10° on the x-axis to the right, press 8 on the numeric keypad.
• To rotate the object by 10° on the y-axis to the left, press 4 on the numeric keypad.
To rotate the object by 10° on the y-axis to the right, press 5 on the numeric keypad.
Rotate Objects in the Scene
10-928 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To rotate the object by 10° on the z-axis to the left, press 1 on the numeric keypad.
To rotate the object by 10° on the z-axis to the right, press 2 on the numeric keypad.
To define settings for manually rotating an object:
• Select 3D Properties > Transformation > Settings for the Rotation on the Home ribbon tab.
• Define the settings how 3D rotates the object in the text boxes next to Axis.
You can either click one of the buttons to rotate the object around that axis, or you can set the axis
yourself.
• To rotate the object around an arbitrary axis, defined by the x-component, y-component and z-
component of this axis:
Enter a value for the x-component of the rotation axis.
Enter a value for the y-component of the rotation axis.
Enter a value for the z-component of the rotation axis.
• Then, click Apply to apply these settings, so that they are active when you rotate the object.
Note
Transformations of an object, such as moving, rotating or scaling it, in one 3D window are not
immediately updated in all other 3D windows, but only after you deselect the changed object in its
3D window.
Back to Rotate Objects in the Frame
Rotate an Object Precisely
At times manually rotating an object with keyboard keys will not be accurate enough. Then, you can
enter exact values into the text boxes in the dialog 3D Properties > Tab Transformation to fine tune the
position, the rotation, and the scale of the selected object.
To precisely rotate an object on the Tab Transformation:
• Click it with the left mouse button to select it.
Rotate an Object Precisely
Plant Simulation Help 10-929
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Press the spacebar or click 
  on the Home ribbon tab.
• To rotate the object around an arbitrary axis, defined by its x-component, y-component and z-
component:
Enter a value for the x-component of the rotation axis.
Enter a value for the y-component of the rotation axis.
Enter a value for the z-component of the rotation axis.
• Type in the offset to the center of the object for the rotation around the x-axis, the y-axis, and the z-axis.
Normally you do not type in another value but apply the presets of 0, 0, 0. This rotates the object around
its center.
• Enter the angle of rotation in degrees into the text box.
• To apply your changes if you are satisfied with the results of your changes, click Apply.
Transformations of an object, such as moving, rotating or scaling it, in one 3D window are not
immediately updated in all other 3D windows, but only after you deselect the changed object in its
3D window.
Back to Rotate Objects in the Frame
Scale Objects in the Frame
You can scale objects in the Frame containing your simulation model.
To scale an object in the 3D window, type exact values into the text boxes in the dialog 3D Properties >
Tab Transformation > Scale to fine tune the position, the rotation, and the scale of the selected object:
• Click it with the left mouse button to select it.
Scale Objects in the Frame
10-930 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Press the spacebar or click 
  on the Home ribbon tab.
• Select Uniform to scale the object with the same factor for all three dimensions and to not distort it
while scaling it. This automatically enters the value you type into one text box into the remaining two
text boxes. This way you do not have to manually type the same value into each text box again and
again.
Type in a value into the text boxes for the x-axis, the y-axis and the z-axis to scale the object on the
respective axis with that factor. Typing 0.5, for example, halves the size of the object on the axis for
which you typed it, typing in 2 doubles its size on that axis.
Note
You can only type in non-zero values.
• Clear Uniform to scale the object with the factors you type in for the different dimensions. When you
type in different values, it does distort the object, for example lengthens or shortens it.
Type a value into the text boxes for the x-axis, the y-axis and the z-axis to scale the object with that
factor on the respective axis.
• Click Set Dimensions. Then type in the physical size of the scaled object considering the graphics of the
object.
