Work with Length-oriented Objects
Work with Length-oriented Objects
The length-oriented objects use their length and their dimensions during the simulation.
Plant Simulation provides these length-oriented objects: The Conveyor, the Track, the TwoLaneTrack, the
Footpath, the Container, the Transporter, and the Pipe.
Plant Simulation generates the graphics automatically according to their settings for these objects and for
the Turnplate, the Turntable, the Converter, the AngularConverter, and the Store.
To create a class from a Conveyor, Turntable, Track, TwoLaneTrack, or FootPath, model this class in the
Frame, and then drag this object from the Frame to the Class Library. You can then insert this class into
the active and into any other simulation model.
You can:
• Insert Curved and Straight Segments
• Auto-connect Length-oriented Objects
• Draw Straight and Curved Segments with a 90° Angle
• Draw Straight and Curved Segments without Fixed Values
• Change the Shape of a Segment
• Create a Curved Object with SimTalk Commands
Work with Length-oriented Objects
