Create a Curved Object with SimTalk Commands
You can also create a curved object with the SimTalk commands.
To do so, use the methods derive and duplicate.
var obj := .Materialflow.Conveyor.derive(.Models.Frame)
obj.Coordinate3D := [5, 5, 0]
var obj1 := .Materialflow.Conveyor.derive(.Models.Frame)
obj1.Coordinate3D := [1, 1, 0]
Reuse the Segments of a Length-oriented Object shows how to use the methods getCurveSegments
[SimTalk] and setCurveSegments [SimTalk].
Back to Work with Length-oriented Objects
Reuse the Segments of a Length-oriented Object
For smaller segments tables you can open two simulation models at the same time, copy the values in one
model and paste them into the segments table of the other model. This way you do not have to type in the
values a second time.
In the example below we copy the values of a feeder line for a Drain from a German model to an English
model.
Create a Curved Object with SimTalk Commands
Plant Simulation Help 10-953
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

We copied the values of the individual cells in the German table and pasted them into the respective cell in
the English table. As the English table originally only has three rows, we clicked the right mouse button in
the index of row 2 and selected Append Row. This appended an empty row below row 2. Then we copied
and pasted the remaining values and clicked OK.
To transfer the segments table of a curved object from one Frame to another Frame in the same
simulation model, we write the segments table into a Variable with a Method. Then, we copy this
Variable and paste it into the other Frame.
Reuse the Segments of a Length-oriented Object
10-954 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To export the segments table:
• Program a Method to export the coordinates of the curved object into a table with the method
getCurveSegments [SimTalk]. Enter the following source code into the method which we named
exportMySegments:
Conveyor.getCurveSegments(MySegmentsVariable)
Executing the method, exportMySegments in our example, writes this data into the Variable named
MySegmentsVariable.
Clicking Open opens the segments table. Here you can view and check the values of the segments
table.
Reuse the Segments of a Length-oriented Object
Plant Simulation Help 10-955
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To import the segments table into another Frame in the same simulation model:
• Insert a Conveyor of any shape into the other Frame.
• Copy the Variable, MySegmentsVariable in our example, and paste it into that Frame, Model1 in our
example. Then, insert a Method into Model1. We named our method importSegments.
• Program the Method with the method setCurveSegments [SimTalk] to overwrite the settings of the
Conveyor, which we inserted, with the exported settings. Run the Method.
Conveyor.setCurveSegments(MySegmentsVariable)
If you want to use these settings in another simulation model, insert a DataTable into that model. Save
the segments table, MySegmentsVariable in our example, as an object file(.psobj). You can then import
the exported segments into a DataTable in the other simulation model and reuse it there.
Reuse the Segments of a Length-oriented Object
10-956 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

