Edit Length-oriented Objects with the Mouse
You can edit the shape and the dimensions of the length-oriented objects and of the Store with the mouse.
To do so, click Show Manipulators 
  on the Edit ribbon tab. This shows all manipulators of the
objects. Then, click one of the manipulators with the left mouse button and drag the mouse to the new
position and release the mouse button.
The appearance of the manipulator differs from object to object. For the length-oriented objects the
manipulator at the start and at the end of the object is cut off. When you attach an object of the same type
to the other object, the two combined halves result in a complete manipulator again. When you move the
mouse over a manipulator, Plant Simulation shows a tooltip.
These examples show what you can accomplish with the manipulators:
• Here we selected Anchor Point 3 of the TwoLaneTrack and dragged the mouse to the left to shorten the
first segment.
Edit Length-oriented Objects with the Mouse
10-958 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Here we selected Anchor Point 3 of the Conveyor, we held down Ctrl and pressed the Up arrow. This
moves the anchor point and thus this part of the Conveyor up. This way you can raise individual
segments, for example to allow Workers to walk underneath them or to allow forklifts to pass
underneath. Hold down Ctrl and the Up arrow repeatedly to move the anchor point step-by-step.
• Here we selected the Top right corner of the Store and dragged the mouse to the top right to enlarge
the graphic of the Store. The changed size is reflected in the width and the depth of the Store and in
the length and the width of the animation area.
To rotate the Store around its center, click the rotation manipulator and drag the mouse to the left or to
the right.
Edit Length-oriented Objects with the Mouse
Plant Simulation Help 10-959
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

