Editing Length-oriented Objects with Keyboard Keys
Edit Length-oriented Objects with Keyboard Keys
You can edit length-oriented objects with keyboard keys.
You can:
• Edit Manipulators with Keyboard Keys
• Move Sensors with Keyboard Keys
Back to Work with Length-oriented Objects
Compare Keyboard Shortcuts for Inserting Straight and Curved Segments of an Object
Compare Move an Object With Keyboard Keys
Edit Manipulators with Keyboard Keys
You can use Page Up to lengthen the selected manipulator and to shorten it with the Page Down.
• Select the first manipulator of a length-oriented object and press Page Up to lengthen the
neighboring segment toward this manipulator.
Page Up lengthens a linear segment in a linear way.
It increases the curve angle for a horizontal curved segment.
It has no effect on a vertical curved segment.
Video on YouTube
10-960 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Select the last manipulator of a length-oriented object and press Page Up to shorten the neighboring
segment toward this manipulator.
Page Up shortens a linear segment in a linear way.
It decreases the curve angle for a horizontal curved segment.
It has no effect on a horizontal curved segment.
• Select the first manipulator of a length-oriented object and press Page Down to shorten the
neighboring segment toward this manipulator.
Page Down shortens a linear segment in a linear way.
It decreases the curve angle for a horizontal curved segment. It has no effect on a vertical curved
segment.
Select the last manipulator of a length-oriented object and press Page Down and to lengthen the
neighboring segment toward this manipulator.
Page Down lengthens a linear segment. It increases the curve angle for a horizontal curved segment. It
has no effect on a vertical curved segment.
Back to Edit Length-oriented Objects with Keyboard Keys
Edit Manipulators with Keyboard Keys
Plant Simulation Help 10-961
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Move Sensors with Keyboard Keys
You can use Page Up and Page Down to move sensors.
• Select a sensor and press Page Up to move the sensor to the left. The left arrow does the same.
• Select a sensor and press the Page Down to move the sensor to the right. The right arrow does the
same.
Back to Edit Length-oriented Objects with Keyboard Keys
Edit Length-oriented Objects Precisely
You can change the length-oriented objects in your simulation model precisely by by entering exact values
into the text boxes into a dialog.
For some purposes this is not accurate enough though. If this is the case, you can edit the position, the
rotation, and the scaling of the object in the dialog Edit 3D Properties on the Tab Transformation and
on the tab Appearance of the Length-oriented Objects, by entering exact values into the text boxes.
• Select the object that you want to edit.
• Press the spacebar or click 
  on the Home ribbon tab and click the tab Transformation.
• Edit the values of the position, the rotation, and the scaling.
• Click Apply to apply your changes once you are satisfied with the results.
• If necessary, you can edit additional settings on the tab Appearance.
Move Sensors with Keyboard Keys
10-962 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

