Model Differences in Height Between Conveying Elements
With the length-oriented objects you can create straight and curved ascending and descending slopes in
your simulation model to model height differences between them.
Proceed as follows to model straight ascending and descending slopes:
• Select the length-oriented object that you want to insert into the Frame. In our example we insert a
Conveyor that is 4 meters long. Then, click Show Manipulators on the 3D ribbon tab to show the
manipulators.
Model Differences in Height Between Conveying Elements
Plant Simulation Help 10-963
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Click the right manipulator with the right mouse button, hold down Ctrl and press the Up arrow until
the right side of the Conveyor has the required height.
• To append a segment to the ascending slope, click the Conveyor with the right mouse button and select
Segments > Append.
• Type in the radius and the angle of the segment into the dialog Line/Arc Parameters. Click in the scene
to append the segment. Click Finish to close the dialog.
Proceed as follows to model curved ascending and descending slopes:
Model Differences in Height Between Conveying Elements
10-964 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Select the length-oriented object that you want to insert into the Frame. In our example we insert a
Conveyor.
• Press the Up arrow on the keyboard to insert an ascending slope, a curve pointing upward in the
z-dimension.
Press the Down arrow on the keyboard to insert a descending slope, a curve pointing downward in the
z-dimension.
• Type in the Radius and the Angle of the segment into the dialog Line/Arc Parameters.
Note
The greatest allowed curve angle is 90°.
• Click with the mouse into the scene to insert the segment. Click Finish to close the dialog.
The result looks like this:
Model Differences in Height Between Conveying Elements
Plant Simulation Help 10-965
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

When you click the Segments button, the selected check box in the dialog shows, that our Conveyor
contains a vertical curve.
• To append segments to the ascending slope, click the Conveyor with the right mouse button and select
Segments > Append.
• Type in the Radius and the Angle of the segment into the dialog Line/Arc Parameters. Click the left
mouse button to insert the segment you just defined and click Finish in the dialog.
Model Differences in Height Between Conveying Elements
