Model a Spiral Conveyor
You can model a spiral conveyor in your simulation with the object Conveyor.
A spiral conveyor transports products upward or downward thus leveling differences in height within your
production facility. Depending on the height difference you can also use the spiral conveyor as a buffer.
Proceed as follows to model the spiral conveyor:
• Click the Conveyor on the tab MaterialFlow of the Toolbox.
• Drag the mouse in the window to the position at which you would like to insert the conveyor.
Model a Spiral Conveyor
Plant Simulation Help 10-967
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• We used the standard settings in the dialog Line/Arc Parameters. If you need to use a wider arc, enter a
greater radius.
• Hold down Ctrl to insert the arc segments of the spiral conveyors. Click several times one after the other
to insert the arc segments. The segments are initially placed on a single layer directly above each other.
We first inserted a straight segment, then added 13 arc segments, and finished with a straight segment.
• Press F7 to open the Segments table.
Model a Spiral Conveyor
10-968 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Enter the additional offset to the base height of the preceding segment into the cell ΔZ. We typed in
0.5 meters.
• Click OK in the dialog Segments.
Model a Spiral Conveyor
Plant Simulation Help 10-969
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The result looks like this:
You can change the settings of the spiral conveyor on the tab Appearance.
Compare the sample models: Click the Window ribbon tab, click Start Page > Getting Started > Example
Models > Small Examples. Then, select the respective Category, the Topic, and the Example in the
dialog Examples Collection, and click Open Model.
