Define the Animation Area of a Simulation Object
You set the animation of the simulation object in three dimensions on the animation area.
To set the animation area of an object with matrix loading space of type Store (ParallelStation, Sorter,
Store, Transporter, Container), of the PlaceBuffer, and the Worker in 3D, proceed as follows:
• Click the object with the right mouse button to select it.
• Select Edit 3D Properties > MU Animation > Area > Animation Area.
In our example we demonstrate how to place cylinder-shaped containers in a storage box. This resembles
a bottling plant in which the filled bottles are put into cases.
Our finished model looks like this:
Define the Animation Area of a Simulation Object
10-972 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

A Source each produces the storage boxes and the cylinder-shaped containers. The AssemblyStation places
the containers into the storage boxes and then moves them on across a Conveyor and a Station to the
Drain.
Proceed as follows to create the simulation model:
• Insert two Sources. We named them SourceStorageBoxes and SourceCylinders.
• Insert an AssemblyStation. We selected the settings below:
• Insert a Conveyor. We used a Conveyor of type Guide-railed belt conveyor.
• Insert a Station and a Drain.
• Make sure that all objects are connected with Connectors.
As we need customized MU Types for the storage boxes and the cylinder-shaped containers, we duplicate
the Part and the Container in the folder MUs in the Class Library.
Define the Animation Area of a Simulation Object
Plant Simulation Help 10-973
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Press F2 and rename the duplicated container from Container to StorageBox.
To configure the storage box:
◦ Click the storage box with the right mouse button and open it in a window.
◦ Click with the right mouse button into the background of the window and select Exchange Graphics.
We selected the storage box below.
Click Yes in the message dialog that Plant Simulation shows.
As you remember the s3D files do not only contain the graphic of the object, but also information
about its dimensions and animation data.
Define the Animation Area of a Simulation Object
10-974 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If you click No, Plant Simulation does not apply the adjustments of the dimensions of the storage box
and scales it to the current size of the MU named Container, as the check box Scale Automatically on
the tab Transformation is selected by default.
◦ Type in the dimensions in the X-Dimension, Y-Dimension, and Z-Dimension, that set its capacity.
• Press F2 and rename the duplicated part to Canister.
To configure our Canister:
◦ Click the Canister with the right mouse button and open it in 3D.
◦ Click the default graphic of the Part and delete it. We are going to create our own graphic for our
Canister.
Click the Edit ribbon tab and click Cylinder. Type in the values below. Click Create. Make sure that our
Canister is placed on the origin of the grid.
