Adapt the 3D Model to the 2D Model
When you created your simulation model in 2D in a 2D and 3D model while 3D was active and when
your model contains a Frame containing objects, you might be surprised how the model looks with the
standard settings in 3D.
In our sample model the Frame contains two Interfaces and a Station.
Previous Scene
Plant Simulation Help 10-983
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If Show Content is active, the content of the Frame, i.e., the Interfaces and the Station, are shown on
the same layer as the other material flow objects. This might look strange at first sight, compare the first
screenshot.
To make the 3D model look like the 2D model, we clear the check box Show Content.
Adapt the 3D Model to the 2D Model
